# KV Cache
When we give a prompt to the LLm then it need to process it so while  processing it goes through various transformers where there is 'Query (Q), Key(K), Value(V).
In it Q is multiplied by the Transpose of K to get the attention matrix and then the attention matrix is multiplied by the value to get contex matrix and then it provides Latest token.

So when we get the new token we have to predict a next token so while predicting the next token we can use the previous keys and values rather than making a new one.
This is called as KV Cache.

# Prefill
When the LLM gets the first prompt and uses the transformer and the Key and Value matrix for the first time for prediction then that is called as Prefill.

# Decoding
When the LLM uses the key and value for the next time and genrating the token one after the other then it is called as Decoding.
The priority is always gien to the Decoding then Prefilling.

